[[�"MThere are places that you can't get to without clearing some vegetation."AI think there's a man in this town that's an expert on that."0It's a collection of rare Pokémon fossils!"9Professor Birch's Handy Guide to Pokémon Behaviors:"~When a Pokémon notices a Trainer, its behavior often changes. These behaviors can be classified into several different types."Read more?"�Some curious Pokémon seek to get closer to wandering Trainers without initiating a battle while more shy Pokémon prefer to stay at a safe distance."}More territorial Pokémon such as Poochyena will slowly approach Trainers as a warning and attack them if they don't back up."�Some aggressive Pokémon will chase after Trainers the moment they notice them. Those Pokémon should only be observed at a safe distance."[Of course, every Pokémon is different and some also behave in completely unique ways."3It's a stack of books about Pokémon battling!"qWhenever it stormed, small blue Pokémon with big ears would gather up north to stock up on the electricity."nIt's the work calendar of one of the Devon Corp. employees. It seems like they're in a meeting right now!"DI traded a Pokémon with another trainer I met on my adventure.">But I need to get more Gym Badges for it to listen to me."^I recall seeing an elegant Ghost Pokémon in the fog near the beach up north in my youth."/I wonder if it's still around to this day."7The shelves are stacked with books about Pokémon!"?It's a bunch of code. You can't really make out any of it."GSome Pokémon only come out at night. That's what my teacher said!"hMy dad's a real ace in the Devon Corporation, I'll have you know! It's no wonder I'm an ace myself!"CHere. I'll give you somehing that an Ace Trainer like me uses!"JIf you have a Pokémon hold a Float Stone, its weight will be halved."^It'll probably be a while before you can use something like this as well as I can though."5Fused Pokémon: A Handy Guide to Pokémon Fusion"`If you get a Gym Badge, you're allowed to participate in Wonder Trades in Pokémon Centers."=You can get Pokémon from all around the world that way!"1Hello, and welcome to the Devon Corporation."GWe produce all kinds of items and medicine that enhance your life."Meooww!"aIf you find a Pokémon fossil somewhere, you can bring it to Devon Corp to have it examined."SThe Gym Leader, Roxanne, knows a lot about Pokémon. She's really strong, too!"S...As I was saying outside, Devon Corporation is Hoenn's largest tech company."SWe started off as a simple mining company years ago, and now we do everything."PTrainer products, new technologies, energy, space exploration, you name it!"rWe even do research on Pokémon fusion! In fact, all of those fields are more connected than one might think."a\PN, I must thank you for helping me, not once, but twice. You really are a special trainer!";Now, I want you to know I'm a president you can trust."CTo thank you for helping me, I want to give you this for free!"pAs long as this is on, any experience you obtain during Pokémon battles will go towards your entire party."7This should help a lot for training your Pokémon."LMr. Stone, there's a call for you from Mossdeep Space Center on Line 1." Mossdeep Space Center, huh?"@Excuse me \PN, I have to take this. It'll just be a moment."Hello? Mr. Stone speaking."Hmm..."Oh no!!""And are you completely sure??"VIt was only supposed to pass by! Double check your calculations! This can't be..."[...Very well... I'll send them the parts. Let's hope there is still time to prepare..."TI'm sorry about that, \PN... That was... Umm... Nothing for you to worry about.",Although, I do have a favor to ask you."[Those parts you recovered are an important component for a... uh... vital new project."YCould I get you to deliver it to the \C[1]Shipyard\C[0] in \C[1]Slateport City\C[0]?",Please, I will repay you for the favor."KThank you! You'll have to cross the sea to reach Slateport, of course."{I'll ask \C[1]Mr. Briney\C[0], the old sailor who lives in tha