ese quests like I asked you! Just \V[2] more!"N\PN! The first episode of Season Two just aired and the critics loved it!"uI can't believe it! After all these low-ratings at the end of the last season! Maybe there's hope for this show."JAh yes, do you have the completed quests I need for the next episode?"AIncredible! You might just be the saving grace of this show!"5Let's see... Oh yeah, this should win them over!"|By the way, the critics were so impressed with the jump in quality for the new episode that they sent us a little gift."I think you deserve it!"4Alright, let's get started on the next episode!"GWe're off to a good start, but we gotta keep the viewers invested."wI'll need \C[1]\V[3]\C[0] more completed quests for that episode! That's \C[1]\V[1]\C[0] total in your Quests app!"Think you can manage that?"?\PN! The second episode just aired and the reviews are in."-Its....\|...\...Overwhelmingly positive!"ZLet's keep the momentum going! Do you have the completed quests for the next episode?"Let's take a look..."IHah! This should be an interesting plot point. Yes, this is perfect!"ZOh yeah, this came in the mail after Episode Two aired. I guess we have fan mail now!"yWe gotta keep the pace! I'll need \C[1]\V[3]\C[0] more quests for the next episode, that's \C[1]\V[1]\C[0] in total!"-I'm sure you can handle that, good luck!"3\PN! The reviews are in for the third episode!"RThis time, it was a bit more mixed... People said there wasn't enough action."oWe're toast if viewership starts going down again. We gotta make sure to make up for it with the next one."hLet's try to make the best episode of the show so far! Do you have all the completed quests I need?"Ah! You never disappoint!"[Oh yes, and those are exciting too! This episode is going to practically write itself!"aBy the way, do you really do all these quests for real? You're not making those up, are you?"SWell, either way, the public is eating it up so keep up whatever you're doing!"TOh, we still got some