d to be rehabilitated for a bit, but now it's ready to continue its journey!"`\C[1]Luvdisc\C[0] can usually be found by fishing in the waters just outside of the museum."DLuvdisc has been doing much better now that it has a companion!"Please enjoy the museum."=It's a painting of the Lake of Rage in the Johto region.""Field Moves: Whirlpool""j"In some areas, strong opposing currents collide, forming whirlpools that are dangerous to traverse.""t"Pokémon can use the move Whirlpool to create inverse whirlpools that cancel them out and allow safe passage.""7The sea is vast without end and infinitely deep...":There must be many Pokémon that we don't know about."0It's a sample of soil from the ocean floor."m"Over many years, the remains of life-forms settle at the bottom of the sea, making sedimentary layers.""?"By analyzing these layers, the ancient past is revealed.""?The S.S. Anne is a famous luxury cruise ship for trainers."BIt sails around the globe yearly, stopping at various cities."DWho even has that kind of money!? Just let me through, come on!":"Corsola are extremely sensitive to water pollution.""U"Areas where they gather in large reefs are an indicator of high water quality.""I want a sea Pokémon!"0I think it would feel cool and nice to hug."gA video is playing of a guy wearing a beanie conducting an experiment with some sort of machine..."�"All life is part of a complex relationship in which each is dependent upon the others, taking from, giving to and living with all the rest.""|"When Clamperl is exposed to either a Deep Sea Scale or a Deep Sea Tooth, it leaves its shell to become free swimming.""�"The Deep Sea Scale allows the pink interior part of its body to take over, while the Deep Sea Tooth makes the blue exterior grow.""6It's a research paper on deep ocean environments.">A fusion of two deep-sea Pokémon is swimming peacefully."!It's a sample of beach sand."^"Stones from mountains are washed down by rivers where they are chipped and ground down.""@"They are reduced to grains and end up as sand on beaches.""CWe were told to assemble here. I don't have a clue why though.",It's a display on the flow of seawater."n"Near the bottom of the sea, water flows due to differences in such factors as temperature and salinity.""E"Only a small percentage of oceans has been explored by humans.""v"It is estimated that there are still thousands of Pokémon species that are yet to be discovered in our oceans.""#Welcome to the Oceanic Museum."Oh, today's your birthday?"3Go right ahead, you can get in for free today!"8\GThe entrance fee is $50. Would you like to enter?"\GPlease enjoy the museum."5Oh, you're with that group that went in earlier?"FYou're the only one who's late. You'd better go catch up to them!"Please visit again!"1It's a sample of sea water with some corals."\"The sea is all connected, but the water's quality and its salinity differs by region.""|"The purity of the water around Pacifidlog Town makes it home to some of the most biodiverse coral reefs in the world.""CIf we stole the stuff in here, it would probably make us rich!"Hey! Quit listening!"J"Toward the surface, seawater flows as currents driven by the winds.""Oh! Is that a Krabby?"Look at that Magikarp!"6There's a school of Luvdisc swimming in the back!"FThat replica of the S.S. Anne alone must be worth a ton of money!"?"Water currents have a significant effect on the climate.""�"Fast moving water cools down faster which leads to colder temperatures, while a slower flow allows the water to absorb more heat.""2I get all giddy and gooey when I see the sea!"8For me, Captain Stern is the number-one role model!".A rubber ball is expanding and shrinking.">"In the sea, the weight of water itself exerts pressure.""8"In shallow water, the pressure is not very heavy.""P"However, in deep water, the pressure can reach tens of thousands of tons."">What I learn here, I can put to use on nefarious deeds..."NPeople may not like our methods, but we're working hard to save humanity."SLooking at model ships reminds me of Mr. Briney who lives near Petalburg Town."SThe ends justify the means. People will thank Team Aqua once this is all over."GI want to learn about the sea and use that knowledge for battling."%It's a replica of the S.S. Anne!"Young man..."Young woman..."Ah, \PN, is it?"DThat was quite a tense situation! Thank you for helping me out!"LWhat they were saying about this asteroid... I don't know if it's true."9It's certainly the first time I've ever heard of it."DOh, yes, I almost forgot that you brought the parts from Devon!"1\PN handed the Devon Parts to Captain Stern."dThese parts are an essential component that allows machines to operate in extreme environments.">I don't know why Team Aqua and Team Magma are after it..."yAll I know is that Devon Corp. developed it for a secret project and that they want me to test it in the deep ocean."GAnd it's an urgent matter too, so I should get to work right away!"$Thanks for this, and excuse me!"!Don't run inside the museum!""Field Moves: Dive""X"Some advanced trainers are able to use the move Dive to explore underwater areas.""r"While using the move, the Pokémon regulate their trainer's internal pressure and provide them with oxygen.""W"This Pokémon technique was used as a blueprint for the invention of submarines.""XWe came here for other reasons, but these exhibits are actually pretty interesting."IStern! Give me those Devon Parts pronto! It's for the sake of Hoenn!"(But.. These parts aren't for you..."OAnd even if they were, I don't have them. Devon hasn't delivered them yet!"... And who might you be?"DYou came to deliver the \C[1]Devon Parts\C[0] to Captain Stern?"What excellent timing!"Grunts! Grab them!"Aye, aye!"AThe boss wants the parts, so shut your yap and fork it over!"Boss, I'm soooo sorry!"	Heh!"BThat's quite a fierce expression for such a wee little scamp.""The name is \C[1]Archie\C[0]."TThe rough-looking lot you see here are members of my team, \C[1]Team Aqua\C[0]."CForgive my methods, but we need these parts you have urgently."{I can see you're not just another mindless brat, so I'll explain why exactly. Then you'll be free to make up your own mind."PYou see now, \PN? When that asteroid hits... This whole region is finished!"kDevon Corp and the Space Center want to hide it from the public... But we know how to get information!"MHah! Don't start panicking just yet. Team Aqua has thought this through!"HThere's a way to save both Pokémon and humankind at the same time!"MThere's no need to run from the disaster. All we need is to adapt to it!"GYou see \PN, humanity's greatest strength is its ability to adapt."oIt may seem drastic, but the only way for Hoenn to survive this is to embrace the changes that are coming."@<fs=36>Don't listen to one more word of this nonsense!</fs>"SThis plan is laughable at best. You Team Aqua are nothing but misguided fools."3Team Magma... Ughh... What are you doing here?"fMy team and I were on our way to Mt. Chimney when we noticed some unusual activity at the museum."VSo we stopped to investigate. And what an interesting development we stumbled on!"I am called \C[2]Maxie."fI stand at the head of \C[2]Team Magma\C[0], a noble organization which values logic and science."dIt is true that this asteroid cannot be stopped, but we do not need to abandon our way of life."TAll we need to do is prepare... So that it never reaches us in the first place."x\PN, this asteroid will change life as we know it. We must do everything to be fully prepared before it's too late."NAnd this is why we need those Devon parts right now!\. Grunts, grab them!"@Humph... I suppose this is a lot for a child to comprehend."`Tell me, \PN. What do you think is the best way to face an existential threat such as this?"This asteroid is powerful. We need to \C[2]defend \C[0]ourselves against it by putting some distance between us and the oceans."ZNo! We cannot stop nature, we need to \C[1]adapt \C[0]and learn to live 