 you go! I converted your Heart Scales into {1} \C[1]{2}\C[0]!">Come back whenever you find more Heart Scales to convert!"SIf you find some Heart Scales, bring them to me and I'll convert them for you!"The Gym"The Tunnels"The Pokémon Center"The Bicycle Shop"The PokéMart"The Clothing Boutique"The Exp. Lab"TV Mauville"The Game Corner"The Pokéball Workshop"Never mind"dThe Gym Leader in Mauville City is \C[1]Wattson\C[0]. He specializes in Electric-type Pokémon."�His Gym is located in the northwest part of the city. You can find it by exiting straight ahead and following the road, then turning left at the Pokémon Center."xMauville has an interconnected network of tunnels to make it easy to get around the city. You're in them right now!"TThere is also a lower level that you can access through the stairs on the left."<The Pokémon Center is right in the middle of the city!"XYou can find it easily by exiting the tunnel straight ahead and following the road."�Rydel's bicycle shop is one of the most popular stores in the city! The owner is known to be very generous with Pokémon Trainers."�To get to it, just exit the tunnel straight ahead and follow the road, then turn right at the Pokémon Center. You can't miss it!"wThe Mauville Poké Mart sells a variety of items for Trainers. One of their top-selling items is the Cell Battery!";It's located right outside the tunnel, straight ahead."�The Clothing Boutique is a popular store in Mauville. They sell several exclusive clothes and even offer \C[1]Dye kits\C[0] that can be used to dye your clothes and hats. It's a must-see!"NIt's located right outside the tunnel, straight ahead, then to the right."oThe Exp. Lab is a high-tech laboratory where they can make \C[1]Experience Candies\C[0] for your Pokémon."yIf you'd like to check it out, it's located on the upper level behind the gym, in the northernmost part of the city."YMost of the region's TV broadcasts are filmed right here at the TV Mauville studios."jThe studios are free to tour! To find it, just take a left in the tunnel and head to the lower level."eMauville is very well known for its Game Corner. People come from all over the region to gamble!"pThe fastest way there is to take the stairs to the lower level of tunnel on the left and then head outside!"sThe Pokéball Workshop is a family-owned workshop that can swap your Pokémon's Pokéball for a different one."YYou can find the workshop by taking a left and heading to the lower level of tunnel."!Do you choose this Pokémon?"(This is the \C[1]Transfer Box\C[0]."�This box can be used to transfer Pokémon between \C[1]Pokémon Infinite Fusion\C[0] and \C[1]Pokémon Infinite Fusion: Hoenn\C[0] or between savefiles."�Any Pokémon that is placed in this box will be accessible from every savefile of either game. You can deposit or withdraw Pokémon just like you would for any other box."Transfer Box"Transfer Box (Off)"�The Transfer Box is disabled because your savefile is flagged as randomized. You can still use it as a normal PC box, but the Pokémon you put in it won't be available in your other savefiles"�\C[2]The Transfer Box is disabled because your savefile is flagged as randomized. You can still use it as a normal PC box, but the Pokémon you put in it won't be available in your other savefiles"cMoving Pokémon in and out of the transfer box will save the game automatically. Is this okay?" You don't have any berries!"%Starting up the Berry Blender..."EPlease select a berry from your bag to put in the Berry Blender."#Do you want to choose a berry?"+Would you like to blend another berry?"JPlease select some berries from your bag to put in the Berry Blender."(You created {1} {2} Pokéblocks{3}!"*Would you like to blend more berries?"$Is it OK to throw away the {1}?"Threw away the {1}."Change flavor"Change feel"$Choose new {1} value (max. 99)."&Choose new Feel value (max. 255)."CLOSE CASE"{1} can't eat anymore."'{1} can't eat anymore Pokéblocks."6{1} can't eat anymore of this t