ious Bob-cut"~A short, chin-length haircut with a longer strand on the left side. Popular among fledgling trainers in the Galar region."Short Unkempt Tuft"aA short unkempt hairstyle with a long bang. Popular with young trainers in the Johto Region."Playhouse Ponytail"rA cute curly ponytail styled just like a Happiny. A wonderfully charming style for any fans of Baby Pokémon."Wild Locks"pThis wild mane of flowing locks is untamable, as if it was haunted. This style is popular with Hex Maniacs."High-bun">A high bun, ideal for keeping your hair out of your face."High-bun Bangs"UA high bun with bangs, ideal for keeping the rest of your hair out of your face."Ponytail"2A high ponytail reminiscent of Lopunny's fur."Puffy High Bun".A textured bun tied up high on your head."High-pony"oA voluminous high ponytail that shows you're ready for adventure. It's popular with new trainers in Unova!"	Hime"KStraight, shoulder-length hair with blunt bangs and long side strands."Phoenix Crest"eA bold, fiery style featuring a high, curved ponytail resembling the sweeping feathers of Ho-Oh."Demi Bob"-A soft, short bob with a glamorous edge."Short Idol Hair")A short hairstyle with a flowly top."Spiky Ponytail"wSlicked back hair tied in a tight spiky ponytail. The style was popularized by Gym Leader Koga's daughter, Janine."Steel Twintails"PA half-up, half-down hairstyle that invokes the security of the steel type."Rocket Wave"_A dramatic, sleek style with ultra-long hair swept back into a high, gravity-defying wave."Quirky Odango Bob"?This quirky, cutesy hairstyle is popular with young girls."Nuvema Updo"bA stylish and practical updo that keeps the hair out of your face while you research Pokemon."Springy Pigtails"0Springy pigtails that somehow defy gravity."Slicked-Back Straight"wSlicked-back medium-length straight hair, in a very traditional cut. The style was popularized by Gym Leader Kurt."Waist-Length Hair">Long, flowing waist-length hair with short, chunky bangs."